#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin-recovery.php:172
msgid "With WP-CLI on the server, this does the same:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin-recovery.php:175
msgid "The file starts with \"<?php exit; ?>\", so even if someone requests it over the web, the server runs it and shows nothing."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin-recovery.php:176
msgid "If WP-CLI itself fails because of the broken plugin, add --skip-plugins=<that plugin's folder name>, or create the file by hand."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin-recovery.php:183
msgid "How the recovery page is protected"
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin-recovery.php:186
msgid "Without a valid, unexpired key file it answers \"not found\" and does nothing else."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin-recovery.php:187
msgid "Only a fingerprint (SHA-256) of a key created here is stored, and the key is shown to you once without being saved anywhere. Keys are 32 random characters, so a wrong guess is simply refused. A key typed into the file by hand may be weaker: each wrong try costs a second, and a client gets a 15-minute lockout after 10 wrong tries."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin-recovery.php:188
msgid "A sign-in lasts one hour, ends when the key is revoked or replaced, and is tied to a cookie the page sets only for itself."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin-recovery.php:189
msgid "It reads the database settings from wp-config.php without running it, only reads files and the database, and never changes or uploads anything."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin-recovery.php:190
msgid "Use it over HTTPS: on plain HTTP the key crosses the network unencrypted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin-recovery.php:199
msgid "Create a new key? The current one stops working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin-recovery.php:200
msgid "Revoke the recovery key? The recovery page stops working until a new key is created."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:103
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:104
msgid "Elderward checks this site for malware and signs of a break-in. Scans only report: nothing on the site is changed from this page."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:105
msgid "Start a scan on the Scan tab. When it finishes, the findings appear below it, most serious first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:107
msgid "Reading findings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:108
msgid "HIGH: almost certainly malicious; deal with it first. MEDIUM: suspicious; check it. LOW: worth knowing. INFO: for the record. ERROR: a check could not run, so that part of the site is unknown rather than clean."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:109
msgid "Timestamp and log findings are leads, not proof. The SHA-256 of a flagged file can be looked up on VirusTotal; only the hash leaves your browser."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:110
msgid "Mark as false positive hides a finding you checked from later scans, with an optional note of why. For files, the mark only holds while the file stays exactly as you reviewed it. Download sample saves a password-protected copy (password: infected) for a malware analyst."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:112
#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:1181
#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:1265
#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:1480
msgid "Settings"
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:113
msgid "Run scans: in the background (through WP-Cron, so you can leave the page) or only while the page is open (if background scans never finish on your host)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:114
msgid "Automatic scans: run the same scan daily, twice daily or weekly. They always run in the background and are skipped while another scan is in progress."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:115
msgid "Access logs: optional location of the web server logs (a file or a folder, such as /var/log/apache2), checked by every scan for attack traffic."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:117
#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:1177
msgid "Signatures"
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:118
msgid "A signature describes something to look for. Built-in signatures ship with Elderward; on the Signatures tab you can add your own for a threat specific to this site, try them on a file or a pasted sample, and import or export them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:119
msgid "Custom signatures only report matches. They never clean or delete anything."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:121
#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:1178
msgid "Hardening"
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:122
msgid "The Hardening tab adds web server rules that refuse dangerous requests: PHP in uploads, wp-config copies, hidden files such as .git, WordPress internals. Pick your server, a template (Recommended or Strict) or individual protections, and review the exact rules before applying."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:123
msgid "On Apache and LiteSpeed, Elderward writes the rules into .htaccess files, checks the site afterwards and undoes the change if the site breaks. On Nginx, download the configuration file and include it in the server configuration. \"Check now\" confirms what the live site enforces."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:125
#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:1179
msgid "Recovery"
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:126
msgid "Recovery mode scans the site when WordPress itself no longer loads (a white screen or a fatal error), from a page that does not depend on WordPress. It is locked by a key you create on the Recovery tab, with WP-CLI, or by uploading a key file."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:128
#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:1180
msgid "AI assistants"
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:129
msgid "The AI assistants tab explains how to let an assistant such as Claude run scans and explain the findings, through the MCP Adapter plugin, or how to copy a summary into any chat."
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:131
#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:1440
msgid "Cleaning up"
msgstr ""

#: includes/plugin/class-elderward-admin.php:132
msgid "Cleanup and restore run from WP-CLI (wp elderward scan, wp elderward integrity --restore), where you can take a backup and preview each change with --dryrun first."
msgstr ""

